From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: extend atomic state and refresh fixes to Elden

Extend checked-state bandwidth, shared-CTL flush, VFP-only mode changes
and idle refresh to Elden. The shared-CTL helper keeps its video and
shared-controller checks. DPU13 PPB registers are unchanged.

Elden modes up to 120 Hz share their pixel clock and horizontal timing;
165 Hz does not. Do not arm idle refresh above 120 Hz, and clear an old
encoder selection when re-enabling it at 165 Hz. VFP-only atomic checks
still require matching clocks and horizontal timings.

Keep Elden's existing display power management and bonded teardown.
Earlier iface-clock runtime PM and unconfigured-PLL guards were dropped
from our old kernel. Do not re-enable those branches as part of refresh
support; the combined power-management candidate failed suspend testing.
The underlying algorithms remain those in the referenced Freedom tree.

Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/tree/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a
Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/0190-drm-msm-baldur-vfp-switch.patch
Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/0191-drm-msm-baldur-idle-refresh.patch
Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/0193-drm-msm-baldur-new-state-bandwidth.patch
Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/0204-drm-msm-baldur-flush-shared-ctl-once.patch
Signed-off-by: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
